{"ts": 1791256250.3619509, "type": "step", "step": 26, "action": "messages_send_to_student", "args": {"text": "Yes \u2014 here\u2019s the short answer you can use:\n\nEvaluation for this build should focus on reliability. Use pass^k: run the agent k times, and count it as a success only if all k runs succeed. That is stricter than pass@k, where any one success out of k is enough. pass^k is the better metric here because a build that only works sometimes is not dependable enough for deployment.\n\nIf you want, I can also give you a 2\u20133 sentence version you can paste directly into the writeup.", "intent": "give_answer", "concept": "evaluation"}, "output": "Sent.\nStudent replied: ok got it, thanks\n[activity] t=15 feed 1m", "t": 16, "activity": [{"t": 15, "app": "feed", "minutes": 1, "detail": ""}], "events": [], "hidden": {"concepts": ["attention", "pomdp", "pass_k"], "p_know": {"attention": 0.20282525443759936, "pomdp": 0.20282525443759936, "pass_k": 0.3691804618986463}, "p_perf": {"attention": 0.0, "pomdp": 0.0, "pass_k": 0.0}, "half_life_h": {"attention": 192.0, "pomdp": 192.0, "pass_k": 192.0}, "attention": 0.7216425168345921, "motivation": 0.8089364796632394, "reliance": 0.45602770298460465, "persistence": 0.37480768876559933, "persona": {"learn_rate": 0.3439719309903426, "slip": 0.1, "guess": 0.2, "fatigue_rate": 0.02, "distraction_rate": 0.2920196205727638, "type": "answer_seeking"}, "off_task_streak": 1, "feed_minutes": 1.0, "phone_minutes": 0.0, "nag": 2.19, "seen_posts": ["p6"]}}
